&Q000792

{1 = 1-9}
9=1.	@wPN{Nibruta-lu}, 
13=2.	the son of the merchant @wPN{Lugal-šuba}, 
17=3.	has had this tin axe made for @wDN{Nergal}. 
21=4.	Its wooden part is of @fsux{arganum} tree of the mountains, 
25=5.	a wood which is superior even to the @fsux{alal} stone; 
29=6.	its stone part is of @fsux{antasura}, 
33=7.	a stone which has no equal. 
37=8.	The arm of the man who strikes  
41=9.	with it will never get tired. 

{10 = 10-16}
45=10.	Should it break, 
49=11.	I will repair it for @wDN{Nergal}. 
53=12.	Should it disappear, 
57=13.	I will replace it for him. 
61=14.	May @wDN{Nergal} look after me during my life, 
65=15.	and may he provide me with clean  
69=16.	water in the underworld after my death. 
